      "writtenOn": "2019-04-18T08:17:16Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "You could use C++ raw strings to keep multiple lines of Java code together:\n\n    static const char COPY_INT_CODE \u003d R\"(\nprivate static void copyInt(byte[] buf, int pos, int val) {\n    buf[pos] \u003d (byte) (val);\n    buf[pos + 1] \u003d (byte) (val \u003e\u003e 8);\n    buf[pos + 2] \u003d (byte) (val \u003e\u003e 16);\n    buf[pos + 3] \u003d (byte) (val \u003e\u003e 24);\n    return;\n}\n)\";\n    fputs(out, COPY_INT_CODE);\n\n\nI think this improves readability. Also note that I used fputs() instead of fprintf(), so we don\u0027t have to worry about escaping % characters.",
